munity Survey 1-Year Estimates Detailed Table B28005\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"resolutionSourceUrl\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"https://data.census.gov/table/ACSDT1Y2025.B28005?q=B28005\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"resolutionRule\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Resolve to 100 * B28005_017E / B28005_014E for geography United States in the first public 2025 ACS 1-Year Estimates Detailed Table B28005 print, rounded to one decimal percentage point. Use the original Census first-posted estimate and ignore later revisions or corrections unless Census replaces the first public file before the public release completes.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"dataPointId\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"census.acs.broadband_subscription_65_plus.share.2025.first_print\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"historicalContext\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"label\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"2023 ACS 5-year B28005 65+ broadband share\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"value\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":82.6},{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"label\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"2024 ACS 1-year California B28005 65+ broadband share\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"value\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":91.4},{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"label\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"latest ACS 5-year households with broadband subscription\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"value\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":91.0},{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"label\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"latest ACS 5-year population 65+ with no computer in household\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"value\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":8.7}],\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"drivers\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Aging-cohort replacement raises 65+ internet adoption\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Broadband subscription definition includes cellular data, satellite, fixed wireless, and other non-dial-up service\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Gains should slow as the remaining offline 65+ population is more selected\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ACS sampling and weighting noise can move a one-year national age subgroup by more than