\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Level, momentum, one-off, and mechanism: level starts from the low-to-mid 80s for the national 65+ B28005 share. Momentum is positive because each entering 65-year-old cohort is more connected than the oldest cohorts leaving the population, and the broadband category includes cellular data plans. One-off BEAD deployment effects are limited by timing because many funded projects will not materially change 2025 ACS collection-year subscriptions. Policy support such as ACP had ended before 2025, creating some affordability drag for low-income older households.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"},{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"kind\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"math\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"text\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Prior/update/interval: persistence prior is 2024 national 65+ broadband share estimated at 84.5 from the 2023 ACS 5-year United States B28005 share of 82.6, current all-household broadband 91.0, 65+ no-computer 8.7, and 2024 California 65+ same-table share 91.4. Historical sample uses recent same-concept annualized changes of roughly +2.3, +2.1, and +1.6 percentage points, giving sigma = sqrt((2.3^2 + 2.1^2 + 1.6^2) / 3) = 2.0 percentage points. Mechanism update adds +1.5 points for cohort replacement and continued mobile/fixed-wireless subscription diffusion, minus 0.0 to 0.3 for affordability drag, yielding point 86.0. The 80% half-width is about 1.28*sigma = 1.28*2.0 = 2.6, so bounds are 86.0 - 2.6 = 83.4 and 86.0 + 2.6 = 88.6.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"},{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"kind\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"text\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"text\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Counter-considerations: upside risk is a stronger-than-expected jump in cellular-data-plan reporting or older-adult smartphone adoption, which would land above the interval if the 2025 share exceeds 88.6 percent. Downside risk is affordability churn after subsidy expiration, survey-composition noise, or a stall among the oldest and lowest-income households, which would land below the interval if the first print is under 83.4 percent. An outside the interval result would most likely reflect either a definitional/table change or a large one-year ACS sampling/weighting move rather than ordinary trend continuation.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"},{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"kind\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"forecast\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"point\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":86.0,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ciLow\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":83.4,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ciHigh\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":88.6}]}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}}\\\\\\\\n./records/thesis-analyst/batches/2026-07-21-aging-wave2-targets.json:24:      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"catalogSlug\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"broadband-subscription-65-plus-2025\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":0,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\"}}\\\\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-07-21/2026-07-21t01-39-25z-census-acs-broadband-subscription-65-plus-share-2025/codex_events.jsonl:16:{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"item.completed\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"item_6\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"/bin/zsh -lc 'rg \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"broadband-subscription-65-plus|B28005_017E|B28005_014E\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" -n .'\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"./records/thesis-analyst/2026-07-21/2026-07-21t01-37-06z-bls-ces-home-health-care-services-employment-2026-07/draft_codex_stdout.jsonl:24:{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"item.completed\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\